# The radius of a product of polynomials whose coefficients are a BallVector (a convolution).
# ma and mb are the largest |leading limb| of the centers of the two operands, rx and ry their
# radii, m the largest number of terms of a coefficient (the smaller of the two lengths), and g, t
# the exported bound of a dot product of m terms. All are nonnegative, m >= 1 and g <= 1. Then
#   rz >= m ((1+u) ma ry + (1+u) mb rx + rx ry) + g m (1+u)^2 ma mb + t,
# the first part being what the radii of the operands become and the second the rounding of the
# centers, with the sum of |cx_i cy_j| of a coefficient bounded by m (1+u)^2 ma mb.
kernel:        conv_radius
input:         stored ma
input:         stored mb
input:         stored rx
input:         stored ry
input:         stored m
input:         stored g
input:         stored t
output:        rz
min_precision: 1
status:        unverified
entry:         yes

p  = prod(rx, ry)
q  = fma(mb, rx, p)
w  = fma(ma, ry, q)
ab = prod(ma, mb)
e  = fma(ab, g, w)
s  = fma(m, e, t)
hm = prod(m, const up(4*(1+u)^8*eta+eta/(2*u)))
rz = fma(s, const up((1+u)^7), hm)
